{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971004-mages-vs-sorcerors","id":971004,"title":"Mages vs. Sorcerors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-16T17:23:13-07:00","id":971004,"title":"Mages vs. Sorcerors","content":"I'm wondering, what advantages do sorcerers and other hedge magic practitioners have over Mages? I don't mean that sorcerers should be more powerful, I understand major vs. minor templates. But minor templates tend to have advantages over major ones in other areas. Ghouls, for example, have a lot of practical advantages over vampires, even though they're less powerful. <br /> <br /> Basically, the question I'm asking is, what makes sorcerers something other than &quot;shittier Mages&quot;? If a Sorcerer had a magic button that would turn him into a Mage, what good reasons would he have not to press it? If a Mage had a magic button that would turn them into a sorcerer, what good reasons would they have to press it? I have the impression that a huge chunk of the population of every other splat would very much like to become human again, with the possible exception of Beasts (and werewolves and demons probably less so, but I'm sure plenty of them want to be human). What reasons would a Mage have to want to be a normal human again? What percentage of Mages feel this way? <br /> <br /> I think I might copy over the Mage vs. Sorceror antipathy from my attempted rewrite over into Awakening. The basis of that was that Mages were much rarer and more volatile than sorcerors and hedge wizards, and the magic they did was much more personal, dangerous, and reality-flensing, so sorcerors tended to see mages as dangerous upstarts, and had a fair bit of evidence to back up that view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-16-2016, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:32:56-07:00","id":971013,"title":"","content":"I don't actually have any of the books with Sorcerers or Hedge Mages in them. But some potential points:<br /> <br /> They don't use supernal magic, which means there's no Paradox or Quiescence. They can actually share their magic with loved ones without breaking their soul.<br /> They aren't seen as part of the Awakened community, so they are not pressured to join the Seers or the Pentacle.<br /> They are not bothered by the constant presence of their Passive Mage Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:42:01-07:00","id":971023,"title":"","content":"What's a Sorcerer again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:47:34-07:00","id":971027,"title":"","content":"I'm using it as a blanket term for magic users who aren't Awakened Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:16:25-07:00","id":971044,"title":"","content":"Sorcerer is something used pretty interchangeably with Mage or Awakened. In my games, different characters develop different words of preference for talking about practitioners of magic; I've got a Thyrsus who calls pretty much every magician a witch and talks of the Awakened as one would family (&quot;one of us&quot;, &quot;our kind&quot;, etc.), a Moros who calls them sorcerers, and an Obrimos who prefers &quot;those fuckers over there&quot;.<br /> <br /> As far as low magic goes, I think it depends on your game. In terms of practical effect, the Awakened are the envy of every low magician and hedge wizard, and I'm not sure the Awakened have any particular reason to envy them beyond, perhaps, that their gifts are not subject to the haunting power of the Abyss. That can be potent and useful. Just the same, the Awakened have Legacies, so even that talent is not unique to the hedge wizard.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like to inject that, if there is a ritual of some sort by which a mortal may alter the world (stuff a picture, a dog's bone, red threads, and a needle that's drawn blood in a box and bury it at a crossroads to conjure a devil, say), the Awakened are just as capable of producing it through performance. It gives the Awakened extra incentive to seek out such people, and to be bound to the strange ways of the Fallen World as much as the Supernal.<br /> <br /> So, really, in terms of envy for the hedge wizard, I think most Awakened are arrogant enough to have none. In terms of envy of the Awakened, I don't think any hedge wizard but the most wise and sensible would pause for a second to grasp more power and knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:43:14-07:00","id":971064,"title":"","content":"Depends on the type. I'll point out that Ghouls who are taught Crauc or Theban Socery are sorcerors of sorts, heck its even in the name of Theban Sorcery.<br /> <br /> The Sorcerors of second sight haven't been updated to 2e yet, although you could fluff the MCI merit as a sorcerors guild.<br /> <br /> A Fae Touched could be done in such a way as to be sorceror like, one with 5 dots in Air and Darkness Contract from Dark Eras would be a very powerful Illusionist, especially with the Mask/Mien merit for Fae Touch (which grants them the ablity to drop the Mask).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T19:01:29-07:00","id":971075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971004-mages-vs-sorcerors?p=971027#post971027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm using it as a blanket term for magic users who aren't Awakened Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1329_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1329\" data-vbnamecard=\"1329\">ElvesofZion</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> said. Though I'll add that the ranks of the Orders are generally filled out somewhat by people who have powers and sorcery would be included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T19:15:26-07:00","id":971087,"title":"","content":"Would Proxami count as Sorcerors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T19:22:07-07:00","id":971090,"title":"","content":"I think Mummy has or will have Sekhemt sorcerors.<br /> <br /> And a mage can grant a sleepwalker magic powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T19:51:29-07:00","id":971100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971004-mages-vs-sorcerors?p=971087#post971087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Proxami count as Sorcerors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not on account of their powers can still be messed with via the Abyss and Mages have categorized them differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T20:02:19-07:00","id":971105,"title":"","content":"That's the rub. The (classic) World of Darkness separated out sorcerers and hedge wizards from mages, but the Chronicles of Darkness don't have an umbrella term like that. It's difficult to say what a mage might envy of a &quot;sorcerer&quot; when you're using &quot;sorcerer&quot; to mean Second Sight thaumaturges, Kemetic ritualists, alchemists, gutter witches, god-hackers, and maybe the Purified, because those groups really don't share much in common with one another. Gotta define your terms.<br /> <br /> The chief benefit of avoiding the call of the Watchtowers, I think, is the lack of need for Wisdom. Wisdom isn't recreational for the Awakened; it's what holds the raw power of supernal truth from burning them out as it escapes into the world through them. It changes how you can live your life. Losing your hold on Integrity makes you more fragile, spiritually and emotionally. Losing your hold on Wisdom breaks you. And there are other things, like the threat of the nimbus leaking out into the world.<br /> <br /> Does that inspire envy? Probably not, especially among the kind of people who wield sorcery of any kind. Some might even relish it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T20:53:05-07:00","id":971121,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest thing is not being as big a target for supernatural beings and not being driven by Mysteries, the Mortal Sorceror has less danger (with the possible exception of ghoul sorcerors) .<br /> <br /> I think you need to divid the Mortal Sorcerors into subgroups.<br /> <br /> Ghoul Sorcerors<br /> Fae Touched Sorcerors<br /> Pyshic Vampire Sorcerors<br /> MCI sorcerors<br /> Mage created sorcerors<br /> Demiurges and Alchemist Sorcerors<br /> Sekhemt Sorcerors<br /> Possible the 2e Giest Minor template<br /> Other possible types of Sorcerors.<br /> Because they all can be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-17-2016, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T21:37:59-07:00","id":971143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971004-mages-vs-sorcerors?p=971075#post971075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1329_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1329\" data-vbnamecard=\"1329\">ElvesofZion</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> said. Though I'll add that the ranks of the Orders are generally filled out somewhat by people who have powers and sorcery would be included.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Most if not all minor template magic types work with and are full members of whatever order with status dots. It's not like MtAsc.\u200b I don't see Mages being particularly envious of any of their little sisters or brothers given they're sleepwalkers and you don't have to hold back with them. Because of this they are heavily recruited as allies and watched for as enemies. Damn useful in multiple situations or the ultimate monkey wrench in others. Because no Mage Sight, no paradox, no obsessions. They really can do what they want and not shatter their family, friends or some innocent bystander's soul. They are driven to know something just because or driven to gain more power just for power.<br /> <br /> \u200bNo mage beyond a Banisher would ever give up being a mage to become human because they already are human and Banisher are just a mage that had their awakening go wrong. Transhuman is what archmages are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-17-2016, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T04:40:55-07:00","id":971253,"title":"","content":"Well, it is like MAsc, but we try to remember that the Orders are full of Status 1 hedge magicians and psychics rather than saying so in one book (Sorcerer Revised) and ignoring it thereafter.<br /> <br /> Awakened mages in cMage revised were <i>supposed</i> to be a minority in the Traditions and Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:03:09-07:00","id":971258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971004-mages-vs-sorcerors?p=971253#post971253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is like MAsc, but we try to remember that the Orders are full of Status 1 hedge magicians and psychics rather than saying so in one book (Sorcerer Revised) and ignoring it thereafter.<br /> <br /> Awakened mages in cMage revised were <i>supposed</i> to be a minority in the Traditions and Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I was upset that the gameline just ignored that book. It made sense, and made Awakened mages pop when they were outnumbered by sorcerers. But now M20 went back to just ignoring Sorcery again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T07:54:28-07:00","id":971317,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I will revise mine to maybe say they don't HAVE to be in Awakened society, if they keep their heads' down they could go unnoticed. Makes sense that lots would be though.<br /> <br /> And given some of the definitions of Sorcerer others have listed, I do have some books ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:36:10-07:00","id":971499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971004-mages-vs-sorcerors?p=971253#post971253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is like MAsc, but we try to remember that the Orders are full of Status 1 hedge magicians and psychics rather than saying so in one book (Sorcerer Revised) and ignoring it thereafter.<br /> <br /> Awakened mages in cMage revised were <i>supposed</i> to be a minority in the Traditions and Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, that brings up the obvious question: Is that going to get any coverage in Tome of the Pentacle? I'd genuinely enjoy a &quot;foot-soldier's view&quot; of the Orders, even if it's just a paragraph or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T14:01:57-07:00","id":971512,"title":"","content":"Depends of what you think of sorcerers?<br /> <br /> Do you mean the *insert* kinesis of the CoD rulebook (pyrokinesis etc)? Then those are incredible underpowered even against human.<br /> Do you mean proximi? Then they can be okay, they difference is that they proximi is more focused and less versatile than a mage. Though i havent touch them in 2nd yet.<br /> Do you mean second sight...ers? Then i heard the are incredible weak in comparison to mages, except certain kinds of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:38:05-07:00","id":971543,"title":"","content":"It was my understanding that almost everyone with supernatural templates or merits was basically a sleep walker. So there are a lot of really dangerous sorcerers out there.<br /> <br /> So this is a possible take that some mages could take on &quot;Sorcerers&quot; or &quot;Sleep Walkers Capable of Magic&quot;. <br /> <br /> Power Stat 1 or Above: Scary, Unique magical abilities and properties, Magic is dangerous but restricted in their purview. They don't fear the abyss. Their low magic reinforces a form of the lie which keeps them myopic. You have to offer a lot to pull them away from their myopia. <br /> <br /> Power Stat 0: They suffer from an awful mix of ignorance and myopia from the effects of their limited powers, and are often dependent and controlled by more dangerous supernatural creatures. Difficult to control for these reasons. Go for the independent ones as allies. Proximi are best because they have a supernal connection. <br /> <br /> Supernatural Merits: Its just scary how many of them there are. Many of these types aren't so involved in a form of myopia which makes them useless as allies. They are ignorant but more open minded and can be recruited as servants and assistants. if they haven't already joined or started a cult. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:53:57-07:00","id":971654,"title":"","content":"Hm, I'm considering doing a hack instead of a remake, and it should solve this, since it makes Obsessions and Paradox major threats and generally tries to emphasize that Mages are fundamentally broken people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:56:11-07:00","id":972050,"title":"","content":"Again I feel you really need to define sorcerors, its hard to discuss this without a clear defination of sorcerors because that could be 10 different things or more. <br /> <br /> Is having an intergity stat a requirement? If so that elinimates major templates, but still leaves Fae Touched, Proxami, Wolfblooded, Pyschic Vampires, Lucky, Alchemists, Stigmatics, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:08:43-07:00","id":972060,"title":"","content":"A Mage with \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 fate can cast forged Destiny which can grant, boost, or dampen supernatural merits.<br /> <br /> So you could turn joe blow sleeper into a telepath for example, turning him into a Sleepwalker or cure one of the Infected.<br /> <br /> So with Forge Destiny you can create sorcerors or take away their powers (if merit bases), or enhance their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-18-2016, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:27:11-07:00","id":972193,"title":"","content":"I cannot imagine any circumstance where that ends particularly well, but when do Making/Unmaking spells ever have a happy ending?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:57:28-07:00","id":972209,"title":"","content":"Are just trolling at this point? Seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:10:50-07:00","id":972272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971004-mages-vs-sorcerors?p=972209#post972209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are just trolling at this point? Seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div> Who is this directed at?<br /> <br /> If me what did I say that made you feel I was trolling? <br /> <br /> And the answer is no I'm not trolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:12:02-07:00","id":972275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971004-mages-vs-sorcerors?p=972193#post972193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot imagine any circumstance where that ends particularly well, but when do Making/Unmaking spells ever have a happy ending?</div> </div> </div> </div> If your a Master of Fate, you can give your self a Fate with a happy ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:36:40-07:00","id":972731,"title":"","content":"I mean, if Mages are just super-sorcerers, I guess I can run with that, and play up the whole &quot;gaping hole blown in your soul and filled up with chunks of magic&quot; thing to differentiate them from &quot;person who practices the occult in some way&quot;. That's not exactly homebrew, but it's not as emphasized in the text as I would do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:42:40-07:00","id":972738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971004-mages-vs-sorcerors?p=972731#post972731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if Mages are just super-sorcerers, I guess I can run with that, and play up the whole &quot;gaping hole blown in your soul and filled up with chunks of magic&quot; thing to differentiate them from &quot;person who practices the occult in some way&quot;. That's not exactly homebrew, but it's not as emphasized in the text as I would do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on the exact type of 'sorcerer' you're talking about. They pretty much are super Proximi, but as for anything else, it really depends. The Hows, Whys, And Wheres of the other &quot;sorcerers&quot; vary pretty drastically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}